1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Stay real good.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,440
Good morning.

3
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:41,760
Hope you all are doing well this morning.

4
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:50,960
Just as we were singing together, I just was reminded of how our passage is going to end this morning.

5
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:53,020
In Ephesians chapter 5, it says,

6
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:59,980
Speaking to one another in psalms, hymns, and spiritual songs, singing and making a melody with your heart to the Lord.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,540
Always giving thanks for all the things in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, to God, even the Father.

8
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:10,300
And be subject to one another in the fear of Christ.

9
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:14,080
We're going to talk a lot about our identity in Christ this morning.

10
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:20,700
Paul's section here in Ephesians 4 and 5 is all about how we walk in the new identity of our new humanity.

11
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:29,940
And I don't think it's an accident that he ends with speaking to one another in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs and making a melody to the Lord.

12
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,580
It's an identity-forming activity.

13
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:41,460
And if you didn't grow up in the church or if you've never really worshipped in a congregation before, it can be confusing and weird.

14
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:45,760
But there's a reason why the Lord commands us to do this.

15
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:52,260
We're filled all day long, all week long, with things that shape our identity.

16
00:01:52,260 --> 00:02:01,120
With activities that form us into the type of people that oppose the kingdom of God on earth as it is in heaven.

17
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:04,120
And so when we come and we sing things like,

18
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:08,600
The rain comes and the wind blows, but our house is built on you.

19
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:14,480
It's a corporate reminder to all of us that many of us are suffering in this room.

20
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:20,740
That many of us are experiencing the rain and the wind and the storm.

21
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:28,860
And yet we remind ourselves of what is true, not just what we can feel or experience,

22
00:02:28,860 --> 00:02:36,340
but this apocalyptic, this revelation of what God has done in Christ to raise us above the powers and principalities

23
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:39,120
and see us with him in the heavenly places.

24
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:42,860
And so even when we can't see it, we can sing things like,

25
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:44,960
My house is built on you.

26
00:02:45,780 --> 00:02:49,680
And this wind and this storm and this rain, it is going to come.

27
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:50,740
It will keep coming.

28
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:56,060
But we remind ourselves through songs and through Scripture,

29
00:02:56,060 --> 00:02:58,420
corporately and individually,

30
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:02,900
that what we can see is not the only reality that exists.

31
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:08,320
And what we can see is a temporary reality compared to the reality of where we are headed.

32
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:12,480
That was not in the notes.

33
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:14,840
So now I have to get back to my notes somehow.

34
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:18,740
Um, we've been in the book of Ephesians.

35
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:22,700
I find it really helpful to cover books of the Bible in large sections

36
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:27,320
so that we don't lose sight of what the author is intending for his original audience.

37
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:31,360
And I hope that we have, um, Paul's kind of framework in mind.

38
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:33,460
I'd love to throw up that slide from a couple of weeks ago

39
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:37,420
because I think it articulates what Paul is doing in Ephesians

40
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:39,720
and in many other of his New Testament letters

41
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:47,780
is that, um, he is reminding us that we have been born into a temporary identity

42
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:51,780
that is influenced by the powers and principalities of this world.

43
00:03:51,780 --> 00:03:55,300
The enemies of God that seek to divide people based on fear.

44
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:59,280
We see that, um, face with the sweat on the brow.

45
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:00,700
This is Genesis chapter three.

46
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:04,500
That from, uh, from the fall of God's good creation,

47
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:08,600
that we are, um, we are afraid and that we are anxious

48
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:11,520
and it forces us to divide into different categories,

49
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:14,020
different ethnicities, different identity markers.

50
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:16,400
And we view each other as enemies

51
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:19,020
because we feel like there isn't an abundant resource

52
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:21,040
and that we don't have a loving father

53
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:23,280
who wants to take care of us and give us good gifts.

54
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:26,600
And so we fight and we strive and we work

55
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:31,460
and we try and get what God has given us freely on our own merit.

56
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:35,780
And it divides us and it leads us down a path of death and destruction.

57
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:38,660
And this was the enemy's plan all along.

58
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:41,600
And we said that they thought getting Jesus to the cross

59
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:44,040
was them having their ultimate victory over God,

60
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:46,720
separating God's good design forever.

61
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:51,440
But what we have seen is that it is the manifold wisdom of God

62
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:55,040
to display to the powers and principalities of this world

63
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,980
that Jesus has conquered.

64
00:04:56,980 --> 00:05:00,280
That the victory has been inaugurated

65
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:01,820
and that it will be consummated.

66
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:05,340
And the church now exists as the working model of new creation

67
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:08,120
on earth until he returns.

68
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:10,680
That we no longer have to live in fear.

69
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:14,080
We no longer have to live separated from our brothers and sisters, our neighbors.

70
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:17,440
We no longer have to view people who don't look like us as our enemies.

71
00:05:19,020 --> 00:05:22,100
But we can live with an open hand and a full heart

72
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:24,760
and we can believe what is actually true.

73
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:26,640
And that is that we have a loving father

74
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:29,440
who owns a thousand cattle on a hill.

75
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:32,200
That we don't have to be afraid.

76
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:35,620
That we can live and surrender to him.

77
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:37,900
That we can trust in his provision.

78
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:41,480
This is what Paul has been doing in Ephesians chapter 1 through 3.

79
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:45,300
And as we turn to 4, he starts focusing in on what it looks like

80
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:48,540
for the church to live in that identity, to live in that reality.

81
00:05:48,540 --> 00:05:51,780
And last week he said it looks like a group of diverse people

82
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:55,440
from all of these tribes and languages and tongues and identity markers

83
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:58,360
working together in their unique gifting

84
00:05:58,360 --> 00:06:01,680
in such a way that leads to all of our maturity.

85
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:06,500
Because an immature church doesn't do much to show the powers and principalities

86
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:09,880
or the world outside of our walls that we are the working model of new creation.

87
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:14,680
We need to grow in maturity so that our witness becomes more visible to the watching world.

88
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:20,000
And he's going to continue to zoom into that fact this week

89
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,100
and talk a little bit more in specific terms

90
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:27,200
about what maturity looks like for believers in the church.

91
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:30,080
And if you have a bulletin, I do have notes on the back.

92
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:33,860
And what those notes are essentially is we're going to kind of zoom in

93
00:06:33,860 --> 00:06:39,220
to these two circles here and talk about what are the specific behavior

94
00:06:39,220 --> 00:06:43,580
and identity markers of kind of the old humanity and the new humanity

95
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:44,480
is what we're going to see.

96
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:46,180
I should have walked over to your side.

97
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:47,240
I always walk over to this side.

98
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:48,720
You guys never get any love over here.

99
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:49,320
I'm so sorry.

100
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:50,580
All right.

101
00:06:50,580 --> 00:06:54,120
So we're going to zoom in over here to these two circles of reality

102
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:58,700
and talk about what it looks like for us to mature into the image of people

103
00:06:58,700 --> 00:07:04,040
that are like Jesus, that function as if heaven has already come to earth.

104
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:05,040
Sound good?

105
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:07,780
We are going to take communion at the end.

106
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:10,640
If you haven't had a time to get a communion cup in the back

107
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:13,860
and you want to do that, feel free to do that at some point during the message.

108
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:15,940
Even if you have to fake a bathroom visit, that's fine.

109
00:07:15,940 --> 00:07:21,500
And also before I pray, I do just want to remind you guys about the two services at Easter.

110
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:26,560
We're doing that to make room for people that typically like to visit churches on Easter.

111
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:30,580
And we also know that your friends, your family, people that you work with

112
00:07:30,580 --> 00:07:33,140
will say yes to an invitation to go to church on Easter,

113
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:36,580
more likely than they will on a random Sunday in March.

114
00:07:36,580 --> 00:07:39,580
And so please take advantage of that opportunity.

115
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:44,760
Be praying about who God might want you to invite to church to come with you.

116
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:49,060
And those of you that serve, we'd love for you to serve one and stay for one

117
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:53,760
so that we have enough volunteers to provide hospitality to hopefully a number of guests.

118
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:54,180
Sound good?

119
00:07:55,980 --> 00:07:56,660
Sound good?

120
00:07:56,660 --> 00:07:57,800
All right.

121
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:58,920
Let's pray.

122
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:03,560
Father in heaven, we are so grateful for another opportunity to gather with the saints

123
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:10,540
and in some mysterious way, gather with this great cloud of witnesses that have gone before us.

124
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:16,220
Those who have persevered hardship and difficulty.

125
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:19,080
Those who have run the race with endurance.

126
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:22,520
Who find their rest in your presence.

127
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:29,000
God, we're so grateful to gather with other believers and remind each other of what our identity is

128
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,080
through psalms, hymns, and spiritual songs.

129
00:08:31,080 --> 00:08:36,980
I pray that as we open your word, that we would have eyes to see what you want us to see

130
00:08:36,980 --> 00:08:39,240
and ears to hear what you want us to hear.

131
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:45,340
God, that this church would be maturing into the image of Jesus

132
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:52,020
so that we can demonstrate to our community around us what the kingdom of God looks like on earth until you return.

133
00:08:52,020 --> 00:08:55,480
For your glory, for our good, and for the good of our neighbors.

134
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:57,340
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

135
00:08:57,340 --> 00:08:58,160
Amen.

136
00:08:59,160 --> 00:09:04,740
We're going to cover a big chunk this morning, and I'm going to try and get through it all without confusing you.

137
00:09:04,740 --> 00:09:10,640
I've been confused all week because there's just a lot, but hopefully, Holy Spirit, you are welcome here.

138
00:09:10,640 --> 00:09:12,440
Give us clarity and wisdom.

139
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:15,240
We're going to cover 417 through 521.

140
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:18,200
So if you want to follow along with me, that's where I'm going to be.

141
00:09:18,980 --> 00:09:27,300
I am someone that I, the term that I give myself is that I'm like decent at a lot of things and not really great at anything.

142
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:30,040
Anybody feel like that's them?

143
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:31,280
Am I the only person in the room?

144
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:36,960
And part of the reason that I feel like that is true is because I teach, I've taught myself a lot of the things that I know,

145
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:42,120
which typically isn't the best approach, especially for me, apparently.

146
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:46,380
Two things that I've taught myself are how to play the piano and how to play golf.

147
00:09:48,680 --> 00:09:54,260
Which means that I am very subpar at both of these activities.

148
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:59,820
But what it does mean is that sometimes I can play a few, like I could sit down at the piano.

149
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:01,840
I'm not going to, but I could.

150
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:03,380
I could sit down at the piano.

151
00:10:03,380 --> 00:10:07,760
I could play a few basic songs with very bad technique.

152
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:13,820
And when I go out to the golf course, if any of you have ever been out there with me, I'll hit a few good shots.

153
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:14,940
I'll do it.

154
00:10:16,140 --> 00:10:18,920
I will also hit plenty of very bad shots.

155
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:32,620
And the reality is, in order for me to have the identity of a golfer or a pianist, there is no amount of tweaking that I can do on my own that will make me a golfer or a pianist.

156
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:35,860
I've taught myself all of these bad habits.

157
00:10:35,860 --> 00:10:39,580
I have all of this bad stuff going on in my head.

158
00:10:39,580 --> 00:10:41,420
And so I could tweak all day long.

159
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:42,160
And I do.

160
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:44,660
Especially with golf.

161
00:10:44,660 --> 00:10:46,120
I don't tweak with piano as much anymore.

162
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:46,780
I've given up.

163
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:51,140
But I could tweak with golf all day long, and I'm never going to be a golfer.

164
00:10:51,140 --> 00:11:00,760
What needs to happen in order for me to have the identity of a pianist or a golfer is I actually have to submit myself to somebody who is a master of the trade.

165
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:08,900
I have to let them kill all of my old bad habits, take away everything that I have taught myself, and I have to learn a whole new way of doing the thing.

166
00:11:11,340 --> 00:11:27,080
And I share that story with you because as we turn to some of the moral teachings of Paul in Ephesians chapter 4 and 5, as I think sometimes we rip some of the moral teachings in the New Testament out of context, and the application just becomes make some tweaks to your behavior.

167
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:33,860
And oftentimes Christianity becomes about just making ourselves a little bit better at certain behaviors.

168
00:11:34,260 --> 00:11:48,000
And we study these passages, and we talk about gossip, and we talk about sexual impurity, and we talk about evil desires, and we just look at our lives, and we feel guilt and shame about all the ways in which we are living these sins out, and we just say, I'm just going to do better.

169
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,680
I'm going to sin less.

170
00:11:50,680 --> 00:12:00,500
And the reality is any of us in the room who have tried that for any period of time at all would tell you, we will testify to you that it does not work.

171
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:07,040
And Paul isn't arguing here for self-taught tweaks on moral behavior.

172
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:27,420
He's inviting you to die to your old way of living, to die to your life that is underneath the powers and principalities of this earth, and to be raised and seated with Christ in the heavenly places, and to learn the patterns of behavior that Jesus shows us, not through hard work, but through faith and trust in him.

173
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:36,060
And if you were taught that the gospel is that Jesus died to forgive your sins, now that you are forgiven, you need to start obeying him out of gratitude for his sacrifice.

174
00:12:36,060 --> 00:12:44,000
You learned a true but oversimplified message that often leads us to religious activity rather than a renewed mind and a resurrected heart.

175
00:12:45,540 --> 00:12:52,120
And so Paul's entire argument here, if you have eyes to, if you look for it, we're actually going to read it all in one big chunk.

176
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:57,380
And if you look for it, you're going to see that Paul's argument is actually rooted in the Genesis account.

177
00:12:57,380 --> 00:12:59,180
He's a good Pharisee, right?

178
00:12:59,180 --> 00:13:00,460
He knows his Old Testament.

179
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:02,800
He's not making up some kind of new theology.

180
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:08,320
He's rooting his theology of the new humanity and what happened on the first few pages of Scripture.

181
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:11,500
He talks about darkness and light.

182
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:13,700
Sound like Genesis?

183
00:13:13,700 --> 00:13:18,340
He talks about truth and deception.

184
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:19,980
Genesis?

185
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:25,120
He talks about foolishness and wisdom.

186
00:13:25,120 --> 00:13:36,860
He talks about what it looks like to live under God's definition of wisdom and what it looks like to take from God the ability and the opportunity to divine good and evil for ourselves.

187
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:41,780
This whole argument that Paul has is rooted in old humanity and new humanity.

188
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:46,540
He is not saying you have to do less sin and do more obedience.

189
00:13:46,540 --> 00:13:59,320
He's saying you have to die to your former way of living that was deceived by the powers and principalities and led you to disordered desires that led you to sinful habits that lead to death, chaos, and destruction.

190
00:13:59,320 --> 00:14:02,520
And you have to be resurrected to new life in Christ.

191
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:06,760
And you have to walk in obedience with him by faith.

192
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:09,020
I love how Tim Mackey says it.

193
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:12,480
He says, the moral exhortations are grounded in the new humanity.

194
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:16,760
These moral exhortations are not behavior modifications.

195
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:20,800
They are identity markers of us becoming a new human.

196
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:26,900
Now, we don't have time to unpack 50 verses line by line.

197
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:32,240
And so what I want to do is just read this entire passage with that framework in our mind.

198
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:35,320
And hopefully we'll be able to kind of follow Paul's flow of thought.

199
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:38,980
And then I'll come back and do some high-level observations with the rest of our time.

200
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:39,360
Sound good?

201
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:41,120
All right.

202
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:42,700
Ephesians 4, verse 17.

203
00:14:42,700 --> 00:14:53,520
So this I say and affirm together with the Lord that you walk no longer as the Gentiles walk in the futility of their mind, being darkened in their understanding.

204
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:55,680
Excluded from the life of God.

205
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:57,040
Sound like the garden?

206
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:58,820
See it?

207
00:14:58,820 --> 00:14:59,820
All right.

208
00:14:59,820 --> 00:15:02,860
Excluded from...

209
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:03,560
I lost my place.

210
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:04,440
I got to stop doing that.

211
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:09,640
Excluded from the life of God because of the ignorance that is in them, because of their hardness of heart.

212
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:16,440
They have become callous, having given themselves over to sensuality for the practice of every kind of impurity with greediness.

213
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:19,800
But you did not learn Christ in this way.

214
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:29,120
If indeed you have heard him and have been taught him, just as truth is in Jesus, that in reference to your former manner of life, you lay aside your old way of being.

215
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:33,000
Which is being corrupted in accordance with the lusts of deceit.

216
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:33,540
Deceit?

217
00:15:33,540 --> 00:15:34,000
Anybody?

218
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:37,640
If you guys got highlighters or pens, go for it.

219
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:42,160
And that you be renewed in the spirit of your mind.

220
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:49,200
You put on the new self, which is in the likeness of God and has been created in righteousness and holiness and truth.

221
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:53,740
Therefore, laying aside falsehood, speak the truth to each other.

222
00:15:53,740 --> 00:15:58,660
Speak the truth, each one of you, to his neighbor, for we are members of one another.

223
00:15:58,660 --> 00:16:01,580
We've been brought into this church, this new family of God.

224
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:03,140
Be angry and do not sin.

225
00:16:03,140 --> 00:16:04,980
Do not let the sun go down on your anger.

226
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:08,720
Do not give the devil an opportunity to deceive you.

227
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:10,480
He who steals must steal no longer.

228
00:16:10,480 --> 00:16:16,880
But rather, he must labor, performing with his own hands what is good, so that we will have something to share with the one who is in need.

229
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:27,220
Let no unwholesome word proceed from your mouth, but only such is good for edification, according to the need for the moment, so that it will give grace to those who hear.

230
00:16:27,220 --> 00:16:31,720
Do not grieve the Holy Spirit of God, by whom you were sealed for the day of redemption.

231
00:16:31,720 --> 00:16:37,880
Let all bitterness, wrath, anger, clamor, and slander be put away from you, along with all malice.

232
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:42,800
Be kind to one another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, just as God and Christ has forgiven you.

233
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:44,540
Key phrase here in 5, 1 and 2.

234
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:46,720
Therefore, be imitators of God.

235
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:50,320
As beloved children, new identity has been given to you.

236
00:16:50,320 --> 00:17:00,180
As beloved children, walk in love, just as Christ also loved you and gave himself up for us as an offering, a sacrifice to God, a fragrant aroma.

237
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:08,400
But immorality, impurity, greed must not even be named among you, as is proper among the saints.

238
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:17,140
And there must be no filthiness or silly talk or coarse jesting, got it, which are not fitting, but rather giving thanks.

239
00:17:17,140 --> 00:17:26,800
For this you know with certainty that no immoral or impure person or covetous man who is an idolater has an inheritance in the kingdom of Christ and God.

240
00:17:27,860 --> 00:17:30,840
Let no one deceive you with empty words.

241
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:35,040
For because of these things, the wrath of God comes upon the sons of disobedience.

242
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:37,020
Therefore, do not be partakers with them.

243
00:17:37,020 --> 00:17:40,820
For you were formerly darkness, but now you are the light in the Lord.

244
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:42,840
Walk as children of light.

245
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:44,920
That is your new identity for fruit.

246
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:49,960
For the fruit of the light consists in all goodness and righteousness and truth.

247
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:52,320
Trying to learn what is pleasing to the Lord.

248
00:17:52,320 --> 00:17:55,240
Do not participate in unfruitful deeds in the darkness.

249
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:57,120
Instead, expose them.

250
00:17:57,860 --> 00:18:02,160
For it is disgraceful even to speak of these things which are done by them in secret.

251
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:05,860
But all things become visible when they are exposed by the light.

252
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:08,240
For everything becomes visible in the light.

253
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:15,140
For this reason, it says, and many scholars believe that this is an early New Testament hymn rooted in Scripture.

254
00:18:15,140 --> 00:18:19,520
These are the songs that they are singing to one another to remind themselves of their identity.

255
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:23,980
Awake, sleeper, arise from the dead, and Christ will shine on you.

256
00:18:23,980 --> 00:18:31,620
Therefore, be careful how you walk, not as unwise, but as wise, making the most of your time because the days are evil.

257
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:35,540
So then, do not be foolish, but understand what the will of the Lord is.

258
00:18:35,540 --> 00:18:43,260
Do not be drunk with wine, for that is dissipation, but be filled with the Spirit, speaking to one another in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs,

259
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:50,320
singing and making a melody with your heart to the Lord, always giving thanks for all things in the name of the Lord Jesus Christ.

260
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:55,800
To God, even the Father, and be subject to one another in reverence to Christ.

261
00:18:56,840 --> 00:18:58,220
This is the word of the Lord.

262
00:18:58,220 --> 00:19:02,000
Let's try that again.

263
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:02,980
Thanks be to God, all right?

264
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:03,500
You got it?

265
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:05,180
This is the word of the Lord.

266
00:19:05,180 --> 00:19:07,360
There we go.

267
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:13,900
All right, so hopefully we can begin to see Paul's flow of thought that's rooted in this Genesis account, right?

268
00:19:13,900 --> 00:19:15,360
There's darkness and light.

269
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:16,700
There's deceit and truth.

270
00:19:16,700 --> 00:19:22,620
There's wisdom that is defined by God and wisdom that is defined by the old humanity,

271
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:27,560
where we take from God the fruit of the knowledge of good and evil,

272
00:19:27,560 --> 00:19:32,060
and we begin to define wisdom for ourselves in our own image.

273
00:19:32,060 --> 00:19:37,980
And he roots this whole argument in two overarching worldviews,

274
00:19:37,980 --> 00:19:40,000
or two ways of existing in the world.

275
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:43,840
He says the old humanity and the new humanity.

276
00:19:43,840 --> 00:19:47,680
The old humanity is animated by deception of the enemy.

277
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:48,920
We've already covered this.

278
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:51,500
It darkens our minds.

279
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:56,620
It hardens our hearts, and it leads us to selfish, dehumanizing, and destructive behaviors.

280
00:19:56,620 --> 00:20:01,080
Deception from the enemy is what the old humanity is rooted in.

281
00:20:01,080 --> 00:20:06,600
It leads to disordered desires that cause us to sin in our words, in our possessions, and in our body.

282
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:11,320
And yet the new humanity is animated by the truth of Christ.

283
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:18,020
It reorders our disordered desires slowly by the power of the Holy Spirit at work in us.

284
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:27,300
It leads us to a life of selfless, grateful, life-giving behaviors that lead to life and flourishing.

285
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:33,640
One is outside of the Garden of Eden, and the other is looking forward to the restored Eden when Christ returns.

286
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:38,300
This is all of what Paul is saying here in this passage.

287
00:20:38,300 --> 00:20:42,760
And the key is that faith unlocks a new way of seeing reality.

288
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:44,560
The old way is the sweat of the brow.

289
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:48,780
We're concerned that we're not going to have enough, that there isn't enough, that we're on our own.

290
00:20:48,780 --> 00:20:58,740
And the new way is filled with joy and gratitude and thanksgiving, that we have a loving Father who possesses all things, and there is abundance for all, and we can trust Him.

291
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:04,660
Even when we can't see it, we can believe that He has our best interest in mind.

292
00:21:04,660 --> 00:21:11,600
This is faith in a new way to view reality.

293
00:21:11,600 --> 00:21:18,300
Tim Mackey calls it apocalyptic living versus post or pre-apocalyptic living.

294
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:24,000
This, God has ripped open the curtain of what reality actually is.

295
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:27,420
And by faith, we see a new way to live.

296
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:34,580
And it's important here that we remember the language around response to the gospel, right?

297
00:21:34,580 --> 00:21:38,240
In the Greek, repent literally means to turn around.

298
00:21:38,240 --> 00:21:48,300
We're walking in the old humanity, led by deception that leads to disorder, desires, and sinful patterns of behavior that leads us to death and destruction and chaos.

299
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:56,160
And when we hear the gospel, we repent, we turn around, and we look towards the new humanity that is found in Christ.

300
00:21:56,160 --> 00:21:58,320
And we walk in a different direction.

301
00:21:58,320 --> 00:21:59,520
Repent means to turn around.

302
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:04,340
Faith is less like an intellectual agreement and more like surrender that leads to allegiance.

303
00:22:04,340 --> 00:22:11,180
Paul's argument is that we have to die to our former way of being human and be raised with Christ to a new humanity.

304
00:22:11,180 --> 00:22:18,420
Many scholars, when they read Paul's language of put off and put on, put off the old humanity, put on the new humanity,

305
00:22:18,420 --> 00:22:21,880
they believe that it's rooted in this early church practice of baptism.

306
00:22:21,880 --> 00:22:28,120
That when the early believers would get baptized, they would take off their old clothes and they would put on a white robe.

307
00:22:28,120 --> 00:22:33,960
They would be baptized into the church, into this new family of God.

308
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:38,120
They would die to their old self and they would be raised to new life in Jesus.

309
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:46,300
And it's almost like Paul is reminding the Ephesian believers of what their new identity is after they have repented and believed,

310
00:22:46,300 --> 00:22:50,000
put their faith and trust and been baptized into the family of God.

311
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:51,680
You no longer are that old person.

312
00:22:51,680 --> 00:23:02,200
You put that way of thinking behind you and you put on a new identity that is rooted in truth that leads to reordered desires and righteousness in your actions and activities.

313
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:12,460
Christianity is not about changing our behaviors, but about being with and becoming like the only true human, Jesus Christ.

314
00:23:13,460 --> 00:23:16,660
Jesus lived a perfect new humanity for us.

315
00:23:16,660 --> 00:23:26,740
And he has invited us to die with him, to be raised to new life and to come under his discipleship and to follow his way of being.

316
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:34,020
And it's also important here that we remember because sometimes our translations don't do it for us,

317
00:23:34,020 --> 00:23:37,300
that this is not an individual identity, but a communal one.

318
00:23:37,300 --> 00:23:40,840
Paul's language here continues to be plural.

319
00:23:40,840 --> 00:23:47,760
Paul's focus on diverse unity that leads to maturity from last week continues throughout this passage.

320
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:50,420
And he's saying that we do not learn Christ in isolation.

321
00:23:52,160 --> 00:24:02,980
You and your Bible and the Holy Spirit are great, but there is something about living in community with other brothers and sisters in Christ where they point out your blind spots and they say,

322
00:24:02,980 --> 00:24:05,600
this behavior that you are living in is not like Jesus.

323
00:24:05,600 --> 00:24:06,660
And you're like, what behavior?

324
00:24:06,660 --> 00:24:08,100
I don't know what you're talking about.

325
00:24:08,100 --> 00:24:08,920
I'm great.

326
00:24:08,920 --> 00:24:14,800
We need to live out this identity in community with one another.

327
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:24,140
Paul says that deception leads to disordered desires and sinful behavior.

328
00:24:24,140 --> 00:24:30,620
And it's important to also notice that almost all of the behaviors that Paul talks about are unity-killing behaviors.

329
00:24:30,620 --> 00:24:40,280
He's addressing a corporate congregation who he's just said, I need you to live in unity in the midst of diversity that leads to maturity.

330
00:24:40,280 --> 00:24:45,140
And let me tell you all of the behaviors that will kill the unity that I've just asked you to live in.

331
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:58,320
And the truth of Christ will result in reordered desires, resulting in righteousness that leads to unity and diversity.

332
00:24:58,320 --> 00:25:01,280
So he roots this argument in old humanity, new humanity.

333
00:25:01,280 --> 00:25:09,340
And then he goes on to talk about the behaviors, the fruit of new humanity and the fruitlessness of old humanity.

334
00:25:09,340 --> 00:25:12,760
You guys saw it when I read it.

335
00:25:12,760 --> 00:25:15,720
There's a long list of sinful behaviors in this passage.

336
00:25:15,820 --> 00:25:21,880
And I don't have time to cover them all, but I do think we can categorize them with these three overarching titles, right?

337
00:25:21,880 --> 00:25:26,720
Like sin with our words, sin with our bodies, and sin with our possessions.

338
00:25:26,720 --> 00:25:34,200
Pretty much all of the sinful actions that Paul lists are in some way, shape, or form find themselves under that category.

339
00:25:35,240 --> 00:25:48,440
And again, in the middle of his argument, he roots it in our, in our identity in Jesus, in Ephesians chapter five, therefore be imitators of God as beloved children, walk and love just as Christ has loved you and gave himself for you.

340
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:52,460
As an offering and a sacrifice to God as a fragrant aroma.

341
00:25:52,460 --> 00:25:56,980
All of this talk about behavior is rooted in us coming under Jesus.

342
00:25:56,980 --> 00:26:01,160
I grew up with the WWJD bracelets.

343
00:26:01,160 --> 00:26:01,900
Anybody else?

344
00:26:01,900 --> 00:26:03,940
Great bracelets.

345
00:26:03,940 --> 00:26:04,360
Awesome.

346
00:26:04,360 --> 00:26:05,420
I have nothing against them.

347
00:26:05,420 --> 00:26:11,980
Probably the better way to put it, since you are not a first century Jewish rabbi who's homeless, right?

348
00:26:12,080 --> 00:26:23,780
Some of the things Jesus did, maybe you shouldn't do, like as a father or a wife or whatever, like Jesus had some freedoms that you didn't have being homeless and not having a family.

349
00:26:23,780 --> 00:26:28,900
And so I think the better term here would be, what would Jesus do if he were you?

350
00:26:28,900 --> 00:26:33,680
That is the, the, the key to opening up the door to the new humanity.

351
00:26:33,680 --> 00:26:36,780
What would Jesus do if he were me in this situation?

352
00:26:38,760 --> 00:26:44,960
And I've, I've seen a, a, a, a social media image flying around.

353
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:46,800
What would Jesus do?

354
00:26:46,800 --> 00:26:47,720
He'd flip tables.

355
00:26:47,720 --> 00:26:54,920
Let's just, let's not.

356
00:26:54,920 --> 00:27:02,340
He flipped tables twice and it wasn't about, anyway.

357
00:27:02,340 --> 00:27:02,900
All right.

358
00:27:02,900 --> 00:27:06,580
Let's just like, let's flip the tables in our own lives.

359
00:27:07,640 --> 00:27:09,380
I stole that line from my wife.

360
00:27:09,380 --> 00:27:13,600
Let's flip the tables of our own sin before we start flipping the tables of other people's sin.

361
00:27:13,600 --> 00:27:18,040
Let's like, let's, let's clean the house inside before we start pointing fingers at those outside.

362
00:27:18,040 --> 00:27:21,720
What would Jesus do if he were me in this situation?

363
00:27:21,720 --> 00:27:25,620
And like, really like ponder the life and teachings of Jesus.

364
00:27:25,620 --> 00:27:27,200
Ponder the crucifixion.

365
00:27:28,780 --> 00:27:38,660
Typically what Jesus would do if he were you is he would die to his selfish, he would have you die to your selfish desires and live with generosity towards those who are your enemies.

366
00:27:38,660 --> 00:27:43,240
That's not what we like to say when we like to say, what would Jesus do?

367
00:27:43,240 --> 00:27:49,420
We pick the things that we like about Jesus's life and we apply them out of context to do the thing that we actually want to do.

368
00:27:49,460 --> 00:27:51,500
And that is not the new humanity.

369
00:27:51,500 --> 00:27:53,560
All right.

370
00:27:53,560 --> 00:27:54,080
Words.

371
00:27:54,080 --> 00:28:00,900
We sin with our words, slander, gossip, obscene joking, and foolish talk.

372
00:28:00,900 --> 00:28:06,940
They create self-righteousness by dehumanizing others in order to make ourselves feel better.

373
00:28:07,740 --> 00:28:09,480
This is sweat of the brow behavior.

374
00:28:09,480 --> 00:28:13,240
This is viewing other people as less valuable than ourselves.

375
00:28:13,240 --> 00:28:17,100
And so we use our words to tear other people down and to lift ourselves up.

376
00:28:17,100 --> 00:28:18,500
And I talk for a living.

377
00:28:18,500 --> 00:28:22,320
So you might guess that I am really bad at this.

378
00:28:22,320 --> 00:28:25,760
Maybe you guys are quiet.

379
00:28:25,760 --> 00:28:27,600
Like you thought I was not bad at it.

380
00:28:27,600 --> 00:28:28,760
I'm very bad at it.

381
00:28:28,760 --> 00:28:32,460
This is a, this is a challenge for me.

382
00:28:32,460 --> 00:28:40,120
And this week has caused me to reevaluate what it is that leads me to gossip and slander and obscene joking.

383
00:28:40,120 --> 00:28:44,580
Because I was discipled in the middle school boys locker room.

384
00:28:44,580 --> 00:28:46,340
So I know how to make an obscene joke.

385
00:28:46,340 --> 00:28:53,720
And what it is, is it's this old humanity way of thinking.

386
00:28:53,720 --> 00:28:58,060
It's, I am more valuable than somebody else and they are in my way.

387
00:28:58,060 --> 00:29:01,700
And I'm going to tear them down with my words and build myself up.

388
00:29:01,700 --> 00:29:04,980
I'm going to give myself the, the satisfaction.

389
00:29:04,980 --> 00:29:08,860
I want other people to think great of me and other people to think poorly of this person.

390
00:29:08,860 --> 00:29:10,820
It's old humanity.

391
00:29:10,820 --> 00:29:13,060
Literally, I was, I was studying this passage.

392
00:29:13,060 --> 00:29:15,500
Can I, can I confess to you all?

393
00:29:15,500 --> 00:29:16,700
Can you, will you receive my confession?

394
00:29:16,700 --> 00:29:17,780
Okay.

395
00:29:17,780 --> 00:29:19,500
Studying this passage.

396
00:29:19,500 --> 00:29:22,100
Focused on the words.

397
00:29:22,100 --> 00:29:26,160
Part of it in my study, get in my car, go to the gas station.

398
00:29:26,160 --> 00:29:26,800
I pull around.

399
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:27,740
I'm going straight.

400
00:29:27,740 --> 00:29:30,740
There's a car coming this way to turn left.

401
00:29:30,740 --> 00:29:33,280
And there's one gas pump and we're like coming here.

402
00:29:33,280 --> 00:29:36,700
And I'm like, I can't, she doesn't have her blinker on.

403
00:29:36,700 --> 00:29:38,920
I don't know if she's going to the gas pump or not.

404
00:29:38,920 --> 00:29:40,660
And technically I think I have the right of way.

405
00:29:41,260 --> 00:29:45,200
So I pull into the gas pump and luckily the person in front of me pulls out.

406
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:46,640
So I pull up to the second gas pump.

407
00:29:46,640 --> 00:29:47,560
She comes in behind me.

408
00:29:48,700 --> 00:29:49,540
I get out of the car.

409
00:29:49,540 --> 00:29:52,700
I walk up to her cause I'm a good pastor who was just studying this passage.

410
00:29:52,700 --> 00:29:55,960
And I say, I didn't know if you were coming to the pump or not.

411
00:29:55,960 --> 00:29:57,900
I wasn't trying to steal the pump from you.

412
00:29:57,900 --> 00:30:01,720
And she gives me like a brother, sister.

413
00:30:01,720 --> 00:30:06,880
Old humanity comes out immediately.

414
00:30:06,880 --> 00:30:08,520
I'm like, how dare you?

415
00:30:09,800 --> 00:30:10,840
I'm being kind.

416
00:30:10,840 --> 00:30:12,820
I went out of my way to tell you that.

417
00:30:12,820 --> 00:30:13,400
Right.

418
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:17,220
And as soon as like, it's in my heart and I'm like, that is, that is old humanity.

419
00:30:17,220 --> 00:30:18,520
That is, I'm better than her.

420
00:30:18,520 --> 00:30:19,400
She's my enemy.

421
00:30:19,400 --> 00:30:22,560
I need her to be down so that I can be up.

422
00:30:23,280 --> 00:30:25,540
And this is what we do with our speech.

423
00:30:25,540 --> 00:30:27,840
We dehumanize other people.

424
00:30:27,840 --> 00:30:31,360
We put people into categories that are other than us.

425
00:30:31,360 --> 00:30:38,300
And Paul says, instead, speak the truth in love and use your words for encouragement that

426
00:30:38,300 --> 00:30:39,400
builds others up.

427
00:30:39,400 --> 00:30:40,680
This is the new humanity.

428
00:30:40,680 --> 00:30:44,320
And here's the deal.

429
00:30:44,320 --> 00:30:47,960
Sometimes, self-righteousness coming out in me.

430
00:30:48,740 --> 00:30:54,940
Sometimes the jokes that I make and the gossip that I participate in are exposing injustice

431
00:30:54,940 --> 00:30:56,460
and bad things in the world.

432
00:30:56,460 --> 00:31:03,360
Paul isn't saying that you can't participate in exposing injustice.

433
00:31:03,360 --> 00:31:09,400
He isn't saying that you can't speak the truth in love to situations that are hurting other

434
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:09,760
people.

435
00:31:09,760 --> 00:31:15,460
He's just saying that gossip and slander and cruel joking is not the way to go about it.

436
00:31:16,800 --> 00:31:21,440
And it's so much easier for me to just make a joke about somebody that I disagree with

437
00:31:21,440 --> 00:31:24,340
than to actually go to them and love and say, let's have a conversation.

438
00:31:24,340 --> 00:31:29,800
And oftentimes, we're not in a position where we can go to the person and have a conversation.

439
00:31:29,800 --> 00:31:32,840
And so guess what we do then, brother and sister?

440
00:31:32,840 --> 00:31:34,820
We pray.

441
00:31:34,820 --> 00:31:37,340
If we can't talk, we pray.

442
00:31:37,340 --> 00:31:38,260
We do not gossip.

443
00:31:38,260 --> 00:31:39,040
We do not slander.

444
00:31:39,040 --> 00:31:41,560
We do not make foolish, obscene jokes.

445
00:31:41,560 --> 00:31:45,740
And the most common place I see this in our current cultural moment is in the political

446
00:31:45,740 --> 00:31:46,140
sphere.

447
00:31:46,760 --> 00:31:50,580
We group people into categories based on their ideological beliefs.

448
00:31:50,580 --> 00:31:53,780
We distance ourselves from them because they disagree with us.

449
00:31:53,780 --> 00:31:58,820
We dehumanize them so that we don't feel bad about making cruel jokes or saying evil things.

450
00:31:58,820 --> 00:32:01,760
And it ruins unity and escalates the discourse.

451
00:32:01,760 --> 00:32:04,000
And it has no place in the people of God.

452
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:10,860
And honestly, I'm sick of opening up my Facebook profile to see my timeline full of Christians

453
00:32:10,860 --> 00:32:14,980
posting or reposting dehumanizing rhetoric around political identities.

454
00:32:15,980 --> 00:32:18,600
If you have an issue with someone, go to them.

455
00:32:18,600 --> 00:32:20,100
And if you can't, pray for them.

456
00:32:20,100 --> 00:32:27,260
And if you have to make your opinion known, social media is probably not the place to do

457
00:32:27,260 --> 00:32:27,500
that.

458
00:32:27,500 --> 00:32:32,000
But if the Lord, through the Holy Spirit, says you need to make your opinion known on social

459
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:36,800
media, there's a way to do it that is speaking the truth and love and edifying the people around

460
00:32:36,800 --> 00:32:37,000
you.

461
00:32:37,100 --> 00:32:41,860
We do not wrestle against flesh and blood.

462
00:32:41,860 --> 00:32:46,340
That person and the other political party from you is not your enemy.

463
00:32:46,340 --> 00:32:48,020
They are a neighbor for you to love.

464
00:32:49,120 --> 00:32:52,840
In the new humanity, people you disagree with are not your enemies to defeat.

465
00:32:52,840 --> 00:32:54,560
They are your neighbors to love.

466
00:32:54,560 --> 00:32:58,820
And I can't help but think how much different our political climate would be if every Christian

467
00:32:58,820 --> 00:33:04,900
in America put off the old humanity way of speaking and put on the new humanity of speaking

468
00:33:04,900 --> 00:33:07,140
the truth and love and encouraging one another.

469
00:33:07,140 --> 00:33:11,200
The breath in your lungs is a gift from God.

470
00:33:11,200 --> 00:33:13,360
New humanity knows that.

471
00:33:13,360 --> 00:33:15,500
And they speak differently because of it.

472
00:33:15,500 --> 00:33:16,820
Possessions.

473
00:33:16,820 --> 00:33:18,060
Running late.

474
00:33:18,060 --> 00:33:23,260
The old humanity is about survival and temporary pleasure.

475
00:33:23,900 --> 00:33:28,780
And so the way that we view our possessions when we're in this mindset, it's all about us getting

476
00:33:28,780 --> 00:33:34,100
the things that we want, even if it's at the state, even if it's at the expense of others.

477
00:33:34,100 --> 00:33:38,380
It leads to entitlement and to envy, which can cause us to steal in order to get what we want.

478
00:33:38,380 --> 00:33:44,260
Now, most of us in the room probably don't do what we would typically think of as stealing,

479
00:33:44,260 --> 00:33:47,420
but we are envious of our neighbor.

480
00:33:47,420 --> 00:33:53,500
We find dishonest and dehumanizing ways to make more money, to climb the ladder at work,

481
00:33:53,580 --> 00:33:56,560
to hoard possessions while others around us don't have what they need.

482
00:33:56,560 --> 00:34:01,900
And in contrast, the new humanity is about abundance and flourishing for everyone.

483
00:34:01,900 --> 00:34:06,920
New humans should be honest and work hard to contribute to the flourishing of the world

484
00:34:06,920 --> 00:34:07,900
around us.

485
00:34:07,900 --> 00:34:10,220
Their vocation is to be generous with what they have.

486
00:34:10,220 --> 00:34:19,200
Paul's saying here, old humanity hoards and stores and steals, does whatever they can to get ahead.

487
00:34:19,200 --> 00:34:23,560
New humanity says everything is a gift from God, and I'm going to steward it like that.

488
00:34:23,580 --> 00:34:24,240
That is the case.

489
00:34:24,240 --> 00:34:30,900
New humans know that everything we have is a gift, and it should be used for the good of others.

490
00:34:30,900 --> 00:34:34,720
Lastly, Paul goes on to address what we do with our bodies.

491
00:34:34,720 --> 00:34:39,420
He says, the old humanity is obsessed with temporary pleasure.

492
00:34:39,740 --> 00:34:48,260
Sexual immorality is taking a gift that God has given, and it is turning it into a God.

493
00:34:48,260 --> 00:34:52,500
It is worshiping creation rather than the creator.

494
00:34:52,500 --> 00:34:54,660
We put no limits on our physical appetites.

495
00:34:54,760 --> 00:35:00,260
We overeat, we consume alcohol in abundance, and we put no boundaries on our sexual desires.

496
00:35:00,260 --> 00:35:07,460
We dehumanize people through our lustful thoughts, pornography, and sexual activity outside of the self-giving covenant of marriage.

497
00:35:10,020 --> 00:35:16,480
Sexual immorality views our neighbor not as a person to be loved, but a person to be used for our own temporary pleasure.

498
00:35:18,540 --> 00:35:27,840
And this is why we have problems overcoming our lustful thoughts, overcoming our evil desires, is because we don't view it as an old mindset.

499
00:35:27,840 --> 00:35:31,560
We just try and grit our fists down and say, I'm not going to lust anymore.

500
00:35:31,560 --> 00:35:33,840
That's not what Paul's saying.

501
00:35:34,380 --> 00:35:44,200
Paul's saying is, lust comes from this deception from the enemy that says that your personal pleasure is more important than the neighbor that you're lusting after.

502
00:35:44,200 --> 00:35:51,620
And Paul says, if you want to be changed from the inside out, you have to allow Christ to renew your mind.

503
00:35:51,620 --> 00:35:58,360
The new humanity is filled with gratitude and thanksgiving for the good gifts of God.

504
00:35:58,360 --> 00:36:08,260
We trust the boundaries that God has placed around food and alcohol and sex because he is a good father who loves us and wants good gifts for us and everyone around us.

505
00:36:08,260 --> 00:36:16,320
New humanity people believe that we are not our own and that we are bought with a price.

506
00:36:16,320 --> 00:36:22,540
Therefore, we choose to use our bodies in a way that leads to life and flourishing that God desires for his creation.

507
00:36:24,400 --> 00:36:28,900
It's about putting off the lie that leads to the disordered desire that makes you sin.

508
00:36:28,900 --> 00:36:35,280
And that sin leads to death and not just physical death, but just chaos in the situations of life.

509
00:36:35,280 --> 00:36:44,660
I'm certain that pretty much everyone in this room has been drug into a situation that felt like death because of somebody else's sexual immorality or our own.

510
00:36:44,660 --> 00:36:50,600
It's just the old humanity leading us down a path of destruction.

511
00:36:50,600 --> 00:36:53,160
In the moment, all we can think about is temporary pleasure.

512
00:36:54,000 --> 00:37:00,040
But Paul says, we need new minds that are surrendered to Jesus.

513
00:37:00,040 --> 00:37:04,100
We need to repent and walk away from the old way of believing and we need to believe the truth.

514
00:37:04,100 --> 00:37:11,740
And this is in every category, words, possessions, body.

515
00:37:11,740 --> 00:37:14,840
It's all, anytime we're sinning, it's because we're believing a lie.

516
00:37:14,840 --> 00:37:18,320
It's because we've been deceived by the enemy of God.

517
00:37:18,320 --> 00:37:23,020
We've been drug out of the light and back into the darkness and the enemy has a foothold in our life.

518
00:37:23,600 --> 00:37:27,640
And the response is not stop sinning.

519
00:37:27,640 --> 00:37:32,740
The response is stop believing the lie and walk back to who Christ made you to be.

520
00:37:32,740 --> 00:37:38,240
All of this gets really gnarly if we're honest.

521
00:37:38,860 --> 00:37:59,720
And I don't know about you, but I know that people, it seems like the church in America today, we don't like to talk about wrath.

522
00:38:01,720 --> 00:38:03,760
I don't like to talk about wrath.

523
00:38:03,760 --> 00:38:06,660
Maybe I'll take it off of you guys and put it on me.

524
00:38:07,760 --> 00:38:08,960
I don't like to talk about wrath.

525
00:38:08,960 --> 00:38:12,920
I think one of the reasons we don't like to talk about wrath is because it's often misunderstood.

526
00:38:12,920 --> 00:38:19,080
Paul breaks here to remind us of the consequences of the old humanity.

527
00:38:19,080 --> 00:38:22,900
The old humanity is leading to death and destruction outside of the garden.

528
00:38:25,020 --> 00:38:32,260
And even as we embrace our new humanity, there will be people who are trying to deceive us with empty words.

529
00:38:32,260 --> 00:38:35,380
They'll try to say this whole Jesus resurrected from the dead.

530
00:38:35,380 --> 00:38:37,480
And so you have a new humanity is crazy talk.

531
00:38:37,480 --> 00:38:39,240
Just do what everybody else is doing.

532
00:38:39,240 --> 00:38:41,480
Radical generosity.

533
00:38:41,480 --> 00:38:42,340
That's ridiculous.

534
00:38:44,560 --> 00:38:48,500
Sexual purity, sexual boundaries, foolishness.

535
00:38:48,500 --> 00:38:50,060
They will try and deceive us.

536
00:38:50,060 --> 00:38:56,780
And Paul reminds us here, don't be deceived because the consequences of being deceived is God's wrath.

537
00:38:56,780 --> 00:39:03,720
And again, wrath is often misunderstood and misapplied as an angry and vengeful God punishing sinful humanity.

538
00:39:03,720 --> 00:39:09,480
But Paul in Romans will go on for a whole chapter to redefine what he means by God's wrath.

539
00:39:09,480 --> 00:39:17,800
And what Paul means by God's wrath is that we have a loving father who is letting his rebellious children suffer the consequences of their own decisions.

540
00:39:17,800 --> 00:39:23,240
We have a loving father who is begging us to stay with him and trust him.

541
00:39:23,240 --> 00:39:29,040
But when we refuse, when we reject him, when we walk away from him, he's not going to force us to obey.

542
00:39:29,040 --> 00:39:34,520
He's going to allow us to walk away and he's going to allow us to experience the consequences of our decisions.

543
00:39:34,520 --> 00:39:36,120
That is the wrath of God.

544
00:39:37,580 --> 00:39:41,060
All over Romans, the wrath of God is he let them have what they wanted.

545
00:39:41,060 --> 00:39:51,600
Meanwhile, he's like the father of the prodigal son waiting on the porch for one ounce of repentance so that he can run after you.

546
00:39:51,600 --> 00:39:58,500
God's final word is not his wrath, but his mercy.

547
00:39:58,500 --> 00:40:05,220
And the gospel shouts to us that God loves us and has made a way for us to escape the lies of the enemy that destroy us.

548
00:40:05,920 --> 00:40:11,320
And he has made a way for us to experience the new humanity that leads to life and flourishing.

549
00:40:16,600 --> 00:40:20,500
Paul continues his argument with two different illustrations that build out his argument.

550
00:40:20,500 --> 00:40:21,660
He's a good preacher here.

551
00:40:21,660 --> 00:40:28,360
We don't have to rehash all of it because he's using the same illustration to make the same or two different illustrations to make similar points.

552
00:40:30,340 --> 00:40:35,640
He says the old humanity is like darkness where fruit cannot grow.

553
00:40:35,640 --> 00:40:39,640
And the new humanity is like light where the fruit flourishes and grows.

554
00:40:39,640 --> 00:40:44,920
The old humanity leads to foolish actions while the new humanity is rooted in wisdom.

555
00:40:44,920 --> 00:40:48,060
Again, echoes of the story of creation and the fall.

556
00:40:49,020 --> 00:40:55,980
We've been ripped out of the fruitful garden and we've pushed ourselves into darkness.

557
00:40:55,980 --> 00:41:02,780
We've been ripped out of the place where God is allowed to define what wisdom is.

558
00:41:02,780 --> 00:41:07,960
And we have been put, we've put ourselves in the place of God and we've begun to define what wisdom is.

559
00:41:07,960 --> 00:41:09,360
And our wisdom is foolishness.

560
00:41:09,360 --> 00:41:38,460
And he goes on and one last phrase I want to point out just because I think it's too good to pass up.

561
00:41:38,460 --> 00:41:41,640
And then I can't find it because this is a different Bible than I normally read.

562
00:41:41,640 --> 00:41:46,380
Where's, what verse is making the most of your time?

563
00:41:46,380 --> 00:41:47,620
Somebody help me.

564
00:41:47,620 --> 00:41:49,580
Oh, there it is.

565
00:41:49,580 --> 00:41:49,880
16.

566
00:41:49,880 --> 00:41:50,380
Thank you.

567
00:41:50,380 --> 00:41:58,460
Therefore, be careful how you walk, not as unwise, but as wise, making the most of your time because the days are evil.

568
00:41:58,460 --> 00:42:06,520
And I don't know how you've read that in the past, but when I read that, I often think like, oh, I got to steward my calendar well.

569
00:42:06,520 --> 00:42:07,480
Right?

570
00:42:07,560 --> 00:42:10,060
I got a limited amount of time.

571
00:42:10,060 --> 00:42:12,260
I got to make sure I'm efficient with how I use it.

572
00:42:12,260 --> 00:42:14,700
Again, it becomes this legalistic practice.

573
00:42:14,700 --> 00:42:18,120
It becomes this religious duty thing.

574
00:42:19,880 --> 00:42:27,860
And Tim Mackey makes the argument that the language works better when you read it like liberating your time.

575
00:42:28,340 --> 00:42:31,260
It's the word for redemption, it's the word for redemption, for being bought back.

576
00:42:32,200 --> 00:42:38,980
Essentially, the argument is the old humanity is in bondage under the temporary nature of fallen creation.

577
00:42:40,660 --> 00:42:45,880
All we can, all we can, all the old humanity can see is the 70 to 100 years that we have here on earth.

578
00:42:46,880 --> 00:42:55,180
And so we use our time and we use our time and our energy and our resources to try and suck out as much life and flourishing as we can for this short amount of time.

579
00:42:56,180 --> 00:43:03,800
Paul says the new humanity, their time has been liberated because we now get to live in light of eternity.

580
00:43:05,480 --> 00:43:14,720
We now get to view all of our time as a gift from God that we can use for his purposes that lead to life and flourishing.

581
00:43:16,000 --> 00:43:20,880
And then Paul transitions to the singing and reading and encouraging one another.

582
00:43:20,880 --> 00:43:24,440
Again, it's all about reminding ourselves of our identity in Christ.

583
00:43:24,440 --> 00:43:26,140
It's identity forming behaviors.

584
00:43:26,140 --> 00:43:35,160
And I cannot stress enough that whether you know it or not, your life Monday through Saturday is filled with identity shaping behaviors.

585
00:43:35,160 --> 00:43:44,320
The enemy of God is trying to shape your identity back into the old humanity all week long.

586
00:43:44,400 --> 00:43:46,260
It's the reason that we sing with one another.

587
00:43:46,260 --> 00:43:56,480
It's the reason that we do life with one another outside of these walls because we have to remind ourselves that what we've been deceived to believe is not true, but the truth is found in Christ.

588
00:43:56,480 --> 00:44:00,520
We need to allow him to renew our minds.

589
00:44:00,520 --> 00:44:07,720
I know this was a lot to cover in a short amount of time, and I am certain that I did not do it justice.

590
00:44:07,720 --> 00:44:13,980
But I hope that we can walk away seeing that Paul's argument here isn't about changing our behavior,

591
00:44:14,120 --> 00:44:17,120
but about being born again into a totally new kind of human.

592
00:44:17,120 --> 00:44:26,360
And maybe you're listening to this, and you've been trying to tweak your moral behaviors, but it hasn't been working.

593
00:44:26,360 --> 00:44:31,200
Or it feels like one step forward and two steps backward.

594
00:44:34,160 --> 00:44:42,500
Maybe you've only understood the gospel to be an individual spiritual transaction between you and God that just primarily impacts your eternal destiny.

595
00:44:45,020 --> 00:44:48,280
Maybe you're here, you've never felt like you needed Jesus to be a good person.

596
00:44:48,280 --> 00:44:49,260
Right?

597
00:44:49,260 --> 00:44:49,840
I hear that a lot.

598
00:44:49,840 --> 00:44:51,280
I can be a good person without Jesus.

599
00:44:53,700 --> 00:44:57,920
Maybe you understand all of this, but you're being deceived by the powers and principalities.

600
00:44:57,920 --> 00:45:00,640
You've been lured out of the light and back into the darkness.

601
00:45:02,060 --> 00:45:13,680
I don't know where you sit when you receive this, but the reality is the invitational response to all of those categories and ones that I haven't mentioned is the same.

602
00:45:14,880 --> 00:45:16,680
The invitation is to come and die.

603
00:45:21,360 --> 00:45:25,480
This is when people typically walk away from Jesus after a couple of miracles.

604
00:45:25,480 --> 00:45:26,540
They're like, this guy's awesome.

605
00:45:26,540 --> 00:45:28,580
And he says, come and die.

606
00:45:28,580 --> 00:45:35,000
That's the response that Paul is inviting us to today.

607
00:45:35,000 --> 00:45:35,600
Come and die.

608
00:45:35,600 --> 00:45:37,260
Die to the old ways of being human.

609
00:45:37,260 --> 00:45:42,720
The humanity rooted in deception that leads to disordered desires and sin and results in death.

610
00:45:43,540 --> 00:45:44,340
Come to Jesus.

611
00:45:44,340 --> 00:45:49,680
Let the one who was raised resurrect you into a totally new way of being human.

612
00:45:49,680 --> 00:45:53,400
Rooted in truth about God's good world.

613
00:45:53,400 --> 00:46:02,520
Let the new reality reorder your desires in a way that leads to righteousness and results in life and flourishing, not just for yourself, but for everyone around you.

614
00:46:06,480 --> 00:46:18,360
Imagine how much more effective the church would be at embodying the kingdom of God on earth until Christ returns if each one of us had this mindset among us.

615
00:46:18,360 --> 00:46:28,220
If we would speak the truth in love when we saw our brother and sister believing a lie from the enemy and acting in a behavior that is unbecoming for a child of God.

616
00:46:28,220 --> 00:46:33,420
Church, this is my invitation for us.

617
00:46:36,480 --> 00:46:40,380
That we would embrace our new identity in Christ.

618
00:46:40,380 --> 00:46:45,240
And that we would do that in community with one another.

619
00:46:45,240 --> 00:46:50,140
And that when I step out of line, have a conversation with me.

620
00:46:50,140 --> 00:46:54,760
When you see a brother or sister in Christ step out in line, have a conversation with them.

621
00:46:54,760 --> 00:46:57,980
Kill the gossip, the slander, the foolish, obscene joking.

622
00:46:57,980 --> 00:46:59,440
Kill it all.

623
00:46:59,440 --> 00:47:01,900
Surrender it to Jesus.

624
00:47:03,440 --> 00:47:08,340
The impact that a group of people committed to this way of living could have on the world around them.

625
00:47:08,340 --> 00:47:10,240
Let's pray.

626
00:47:10,240 --> 00:47:17,800
Father in heaven, we thank you yet again for an opportunity to gather with the saints.

627
00:47:17,800 --> 00:47:24,800
The imperfect, broken, and yet redeemed people of God.

628
00:47:26,080 --> 00:47:33,020
Who have been invited to bring our gifts, to mature towards Christ, who is our head.

629
00:47:33,020 --> 00:47:39,300
God, if there's anyone in this room who has yet to die to their old self.

630
00:47:39,300 --> 00:47:44,400
Who has yet to repent of the lies that they have believed from the enemy and turned back to you.

631
00:47:44,400 --> 00:47:50,600
If there's anyone in this room who has not yet put off the old way of living and put on the new way of living through baptism.

632
00:47:50,600 --> 00:47:54,180
I pray this morning that today would be the day that you are inviting them.

633
00:47:54,180 --> 00:47:57,740
That you are calling them out of their old humanity into a new humanity.

634
00:47:57,740 --> 00:48:05,000
If there's anybody in this room who has been trying to become more like you through behavior modification.

635
00:48:05,000 --> 00:48:09,200
God, may today be the day that you allow our minds to be renewed by the truth.

636
00:48:09,200 --> 00:48:11,540
Through the power of your spirit.

637
00:48:11,540 --> 00:48:15,040
Father, we love you.

638
00:48:15,040 --> 00:48:17,100
We thank you for Jesus.

639
00:48:17,100 --> 00:48:18,860
Amen.
